{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["And also יהתיבון — those who reply will reply." "And ויהך — וילך כל כלי להיכלא, and the word is singular from the plural, in the manner of כי יתן מים." "ותחת — corresponding to Sheshbazzar, about whom the letter speaks. And the meaning is: and you, Sheshbazzar, shall be placed or rest in the house of Elohim. The למ\"ד of לעבידת stands in place of two [letters], and likewise is לפחת יהודאי."], :book :ezra, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {2 "The phrase למ\"ד לעבידת עומד במקום שנים is textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally. The intended grammatical point appears to concern an Aramaic morphological feature but the formulation is obscure."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ezra -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:04.935131862Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}